THIS IS AN EXAMPLE, NOT A REAL KEY. It only shows where the private signing key goes.

How to get your own key (see DEVELOPMENT.md for the full steps):

    npx tauri signer generate -w keys/private.key

That command creates two files:
  keys/private.key      the PRIVATE key. Keep it secret. It is ignored by git (*.key).
  keys/public.pub      the PUBLIC key. Commit it. The app reads it automatically (scripts/tauri.mjs).

A real private key is a single line of base64 text, about 350 characters long.

Never commit keys/private.key, never paste it in chats or issues, and back it up somewhere
safe: if you lose it, apps you already released can never be updated again.
